"""The mutations of plan step 10 (the node editor: its geometry, the Tk widget, and Graph.can_connect): run with
    python dev/mutation/mutate.py dev/mutation/step10.py
Every one of them should be reported as caught; see mutate.py. (A name starting G is canopysynth/editor/geometry.py, V canopysynth/editor/canvas.py,
M canopysynth/graph.py. They are all Python files, so the runner skips the build and the extra C runs. Not mutated, because the change is invisible: the
sort order of the built-in entries of the add menu (the registry lists them in alphabetical order already), and how often the editor redraws.
Changed at step 11, with the code they broke: G16 (the width of a title, a method nothing used any more), G17, G18, G20, G21, G23 and G24 (the built-in node's title strip above its body,
replaced by an uncoloured bar inside the node) and V61 (a right click on a node opened no menu; it now does, and step11.py tests that) were removed; the others whose code moved
(G19, G26 to G28, G30, G31, G33, G34, V04, V21, V38, V42, V44, V54, V63) were re-pointed to the new text and mean the same.)"""
